  "chapter": 734,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 101 Chapter 734\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 5082, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the environmental conservation law and the state\n        finance law, in  relation  to  restricting  hotels  from  making\n        available  to  hotel  guests  small  plastic  bottle hospitality\n        personal care products\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would amend the environmental conservation law  to  prohibit\nhotels  from  providing  small  plastic bottles that contain hospitality\npersonal care products to patrons and guests. In  particular,  the  bill\nwould prohibit hotels from providing plastic containers with less than a\n12  ounce capacity beginning on January 1, 2024 for hotels with 50 rooms\nor more and on January 1, 2025 for hotels with less than 50 rooms.\n \n  I agree with the sponsors that this bill would take a meaningful  step\nin reducing plastic waste and contamination to our oceans and waterways.\nA  single  hotel  room  uses an estimated 1,000 single-use personal care\nproduct containers per year, on average, with only 15 to 30  percent  of\nthe  contents  \"consumed\" and the remaining 70-85% becoming waste. Those\nremaining contents in the bottles, in turn,  contaminate  the  recycling\nstream. Eliminating the use of these single-use containers and replacing\nthem  with  reusable  dispensers  is  a  win-win: reducing a significant\nsource of plastic waste while also reducing costs and  increasing  turn-\nover efficiency for hotels.\n \n  However,  similar  legislation  enacted in California in 2019 provided\nCalifornia hotels with an additional year from enactment to  prohibition\nrelative  to the timeframes afforded to New York hotels under this bill.\nNew York hotels should not have less  time  to  adjust  operations  than\ntheir   California   counterparts,  particularly  in  light  of  current\nupheavals in global supply markets. Therefore, the Executive has reached\nagreement with the Legislature on a bill to be introduced  next  session\nthat  will  provide  hotels  with  an additional year to comply. On this\nbasis, I can approve this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
